                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0d298bc2-2f19-36f4-8389-5b26f3fcc689",
                        "entry_id": "e022eff8-e8b6-3153-b597-427a2118ef53",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Technique traditionnelle de culture associée du maïs, de la courge et du haricot, pour une interaction bénéfique."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b5063570-7fae-4af0-8d31-61962da2b7c6",
                                "sense_id": "0d298bc2-2f19-36f4-8389-5b26f3fcc689",
                                "text": "Donc, on considère que la terre est la mère de l’homme. Et dans les faits nos parents nous apprennent à respecter cette terre. On ne peut blesser la terre qu’en cas de nécessité. Cette conception fait qu’avant de semer notre milpa, nous devons demander l’autorisation à la terre."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "13fcd190-6b29-4ddc-8134-992b555554f0",
                                "sense_id": "0d298bc2-2f19-36f4-8389-5b26f3fcc689",
                                "text": "L’archétype d’une telle association est l’historique milpa (ou « trois sœurs ») connue depuis plus de 2 000 ans en Amérique centrale."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "76e994b6-a06e-4bc6-8ed4-c0d6564a1eab",
                        "source_entry_id": "e022eff8-e8b6-3153-b597-427a2118ef53",
                        "source_sense_id": "0d298bc2-2f19-36f4-8389-5b26f3fcc689",
                        "target_lang_word": "milpa",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "milpa",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "24bcf5e3-db07-3291-ad90-c6919f528cab",
                                        "entry_id": "983ee403-ec2e-35d5-acba-f82bdf010a2e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A cyclical crop-growing system used throughout Mesoamerica."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "af8d35d1-0519-4930-82b8-a08110efb37b",
                                                "sense_id": "24bcf5e3-db07-3291-ad90-c6919f528cab",
                                                "text": "Milpa is based on seed crops, particularly the uniquely productive combination of maize, beans and squash, and in the past its techniques were normally those of swidden cultivation."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "09399c8d-6180-3eb3-9300-7d56620cffb5",
                                        "entry_id": "983ee403-ec2e-35d5-acba-f82bdf010a2e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A small field, especially in Mexico or Central America, that is cleared from the jungle, cropped for a few seasons, and then abandoned for a fresh clearing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2a82eaab-3e1f-44d8-a100-14a7b5d47743",
                                                "sense_id": "09399c8d-6180-3eb3-9300-7d56620cffb5",
                                                "text": "These three plants are often grown together in a single field called a milpa, the beans creeping up the corn stalks while the squash plants catch along the lower leaves of the corn plants."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9a5603ad-0b72-4355-921c-6551c8f6ee08",
                                                "sense_id": "09399c8d-6180-3eb3-9300-7d56620cffb5",
                                                "text": "That means that no one can get rich or make someone else rich by farming a milpa. Since it works against capital accumulation, it is antithetical to entrepreneurship. In short, planting a milpa optimizes resources in a very particular way."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
